\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces What recent learned receivers and demodulators are given. \emph  {family} denotes a fixed known pulse-shape family that is not itself presented to the network; \emph  {blind} denotes symbol timing recovered by the system; \emph  {partial} denotes a residual offset estimated from the signal; \emph  {n.s.} denotes a property the paper does not state, which is not the same as a property it does not use. \emph  {Domains}: passband, baseband in-phase and quadrature, post-matched-filter symbols, frequency domain. \emph  {Data}: simulated, hardware used for validation only, hardware also used for over-the-air training (\emph  {hw-train}), hardware as the primary source. Surveys, datasets and vision articles without an evaluated receiver are cited in the text and not tabulated.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
